            <p>
                <strong>2. </strong>
                This question has two parts. Answer Part A and then Part B.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Part A </strong>
                In paragraph 3, the author organizes and presents information by&#x2014;
            </p>
            <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_1" shuffle="false" max-choices="1" min-choices="1">
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic001">
                    <strong>A. </strong>
                    asking questions and giving answers.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic002">
                    <strong>B. </strong>
                    comparing and contrasting events.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic003">
                    <strong>C. </strong>
                    giving a problem and solution.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic004">
                    <strong>D. </strong>
                    explaining causes and effects.
                </qti-simple-choice>
            </qti-choice-interaction>
            <p>
                <strong>Part B </strong>
                Which sentence from paragraph 3
                <strong>best</strong>
                supports the answer to Part A?
            </p>
            <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_2" shuffle="false" max-choices="1" min-choices="1">
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic005">
                    <strong>A. </strong>
                    &quot;During the Great Depression, most people in the Great Plains farmed for a living.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic006">
                    <strong>B. </strong>
                    &quot;This practice was hard on the land because it wore out the soil and led to soil erosion.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic007">
                    <strong>C. </strong>
                    &quot;Winds easily stirred up the dust and carried it into the air.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi002asic008">
                    <strong>D. </strong>
                    &quot;A haze of dust often hung in the sky for days after the winds died down.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
